      "why_not_addressable": "Principle 6 requires aggregation capabilities to be flexible and adaptable to ad hoc requests, new business developments, and regulatory changes (¶48-49). It requires the systems themselves to be able to reconfigure aggregation on demand. A data catalog can document what data exists and where, supporting the discovery aspect of ad hoc query fulfilment — but it cannot make the aggregation systems flexible, cannot guarantee that a new slicing dimension will be computable on demand, and cannot ensure that system changes resulting from acquisitions or regulatory change are reflected in aggregation capabilities. Adaptability is an IT capability requirement, not a metadata management requirement.",
